  "why": "The detector is byte-identical across arms: same checkpoint, same decoded frames, same code path, and the sanity checks confirm 300 inferences per 300 frames with zero cache hits in every run. Yet its measured cost differs by +102.2 ms/frame between arms, and varies by 150 ms/frame within the legacy arm alone. The dominant term was not held constant, so the +20.99% total is machine variance attributed to whichever arm ran during a slow interval, not a property of CBIoU.",
